WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:35.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.068
THE DREAM LIFE OF MR. KIM

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:54.326
Once he's all done,

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:55.827
you take some sand

00:00:56.453 --> 00:00:58.121
and sprinkle it on top.

00:00:58.664 --> 00:01:01.833
Then you just sweep it up.

00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:04.795
And toss it in here.

00:01:04.878 --> 00:01:06.129
Then you're done.

00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:08.215
Do I have to clean up the poop?

00:01:08.298 --> 00:01:09.299
Yes.

00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:13.553
Attention, all employees.

00:01:13.637 --> 00:01:17.057
Thank you for your hard work this morning.

00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:20.977
Lunchtime is until one o'clock.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.232
We hope you all enjoy your lunch.

00:01:25.315 --> 00:01:27.984
Lunchtime!

00:01:33.365 --> 00:01:35.826
You have to run for your lunch
around here.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:36.868
Excuse me?

00:01:36.952 --> 00:01:39.579
-If you're late, you'll get nothing.
-Okay.

00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:41.123
And only one yogurt per person!

00:01:41.206 --> 00:01:42.332
Okay.

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:44.710
Jeez.

00:01:47.045 --> 00:01:48.088
Bye.

00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:51.508
-Hey!
-Shoot!

00:01:52.008 --> 00:01:53.135
-Darn it!
-Hey.

00:01:53.218 --> 00:01:54.177
Nice!

00:01:54.261 --> 00:01:56.847
You really are leaving
without having done anything.

00:01:57.389 --> 00:01:59.099
There was no work for me to do.

00:01:59.766 --> 00:02:00.642
Yes, there was.

00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:02.519
That wasn't work.

00:02:03.937 --> 00:02:05.439
It was just an errand.

00:02:05.522 --> 00:02:08.316
Actually, it was better for us
that you didn't do any work here.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.026
Don't think of it like that.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.278
HQ will push harder.

00:02:11.361 --> 00:02:13.947
I heard they're going
to shut down this factory.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.324
Why are you so surprised?
We hear things too.

00:02:18.326 --> 00:02:22.372
The pressure from HQ will get worse,
and things will get a lot tougher here.

00:02:22.456 --> 00:02:23.457
I haven't done anything.

00:02:24.207 --> 00:02:25.459
Yes, you have.

00:02:26.001 --> 00:02:28.670
You don't think there's a difference
between the world ending tomorrow

00:02:28.754 --> 00:02:30.672
and it ending a year from now?

00:02:30.756 --> 00:02:32.299
That one year is so precious.

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:36.261
Whether we hide underground
or flee to another planet,

00:02:37.095 --> 00:02:39.139
it gives us time to plan.

00:02:39.222 --> 00:02:42.350
And it gives us precious time
with our families.

00:02:42.893 --> 00:02:44.060
Don't you think?

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.981
In the end,

00:02:49.107 --> 00:02:52.736
you did a great job keeping
the workers at this factory safe.

00:02:54.112 --> 00:02:55.989
You should take credit for that.

00:03:00.368 --> 00:03:01.411
If that's the case…

00:03:02.996 --> 00:03:05.957
You could have at least
thrown me a surprise farewell party.

00:03:06.041 --> 00:03:07.501
-What?
-Or, at the very least,

00:03:07.584 --> 00:03:09.169
you all could've given me a card.

00:03:09.252 --> 00:03:10.462
You say you guys are grateful,

00:03:10.545 --> 00:03:12.589
but no one's seeing me off.
They're just playing ball.

00:03:12.672 --> 00:03:14.466
Is having me here not enough for you?

00:03:15.342 --> 00:03:18.970
That's right.
I prefer quantity over quality.

00:03:20.138 --> 00:03:21.431
My apologies.

00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:25.685
If I'd known, I would've
prepared a big send-off or something.

00:03:27.145 --> 00:03:28.355
Whatever.

00:03:28.438 --> 00:03:31.775
I even put on a little show
and made you all bomb shots.

00:03:32.317 --> 00:03:33.693
Right.

00:03:34.402 --> 00:03:36.154
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

00:03:36.238 --> 00:03:37.739
It was so, so good.

00:03:40.116 --> 00:03:42.035
Just keep thinking about it, then.

00:03:43.328 --> 00:03:45.080
Because you'll never have it again.

00:03:47.123 --> 00:03:48.124
I'm going now.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.877
Can I have your business card?

00:03:53.255 --> 00:03:55.131
Your timing is ridiculous.

00:03:55.882 --> 00:03:57.300
Just give me one anyway.

00:04:03.265 --> 00:04:04.683
ACT Sales Team 1--

00:04:10.522 --> 00:04:11.439
I'm Kim Nak-su.

00:04:13.191 --> 00:04:17.362
I'm Lee Ju-young,
the Production Team Supervisor.

00:04:23.285 --> 00:04:24.619
GENERAL MANAGER KIM NAK-SU

00:04:24.703 --> 00:04:26.037
PRODUCTION TEAM
LEE JU-YOUNG

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.733
Thank you for your hard work, Mr. Kim!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.568
Yes.

00:04:56.651 --> 00:04:58.028
Good luck. Thank you.

00:04:58.904 --> 00:05:00.864
Thank you for your hard work.

00:05:00.947 --> 00:05:01.823
Thank you.

00:05:01.907 --> 00:05:03.783
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:05:14.169 --> 00:05:16.212
ACT EMPLOYEE DORMITORY

00:05:32.896 --> 00:05:36.024
EPISODE 8
ALL IN

00:05:36.107 --> 00:05:37.233
KIM NAK-SU HAS LEFT THE CHAT

00:05:37.317 --> 00:05:38.401
Mr. Kim left the…

00:05:40.028 --> 00:05:42.489
-Mr. Do, did you enjoy your--
-You're back from lunch.

00:05:42.572 --> 00:05:44.658
-Did you have a good lunch?
-Sleep some more.

00:05:44.741 --> 00:05:47.869
-The lunch break isn't over yet.
-No, sir. I was brainstorming.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.748
Did you know Mr. Kim Nak-su came up
with the idea of public Wi-Fi zones

00:05:51.831 --> 00:05:54.376
and insisted that we expand on them?

00:05:56.461 --> 00:05:58.505
Really? He was a legend.

00:05:58.588 --> 00:06:02.133
He was someone to look up to.
It's a shame how things turned out.

00:06:02.217 --> 00:06:03.718
Is something wrong?

00:06:04.386 --> 00:06:05.679
You didn't know either?

00:06:06.429 --> 00:06:08.723
Mr. Kim left the company today.

00:06:09.432 --> 00:06:11.643
-What?
-That's why he left the group chat.

00:06:11.726 --> 00:06:14.813
If he'd given us a heads-up,
we could've thrown a farewell party.

00:06:14.896 --> 00:06:18.900
It's a shame.
We didn't even get to say goodbye.

00:06:18.984 --> 00:06:23.363
Well, people come and go.
That's how it is.

00:06:23.446 --> 00:06:26.324
Sir, there's an issue
with the main conference room.

00:06:26.408 --> 00:06:28.618
-We've moved the meeting to Room A.
-Okay. Let's go.

00:06:28.702 --> 00:06:29.703
Are you going somewhere?

00:06:29.786 --> 00:06:31.871
-Did we have a meeting this afternoon?
-No.

00:06:31.955 --> 00:06:34.833
Team 1 doesn't need to attend,
so I didn't tell you.

00:06:34.916 --> 00:06:37.460
I'll have Myung-heon fill you in
on anything you may need to know.

00:06:37.544 --> 00:06:38.670
From now on.

00:06:38.753 --> 00:06:40.422
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

00:06:40.505 --> 00:06:41.506
Yes, sir.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.511
What was that just now?

00:06:46.594 --> 00:06:50.223
He's letting us know
we're just Kim Nak-su's guys.

00:07:13.079 --> 00:07:14.581
Breakfast is ready!

00:07:14.664 --> 00:07:15.540
Okay.

00:07:15.623 --> 00:07:17.417
Su-gyeom, let's eat.

00:07:21.337 --> 00:07:22.213
This is delicious.

00:07:22.297 --> 00:07:23.631
What's gotten into you?

00:07:23.715 --> 00:07:26.092
Seriously, this is amazing.
Su-gyeom, try some.

00:07:26.176 --> 00:07:30.138
Honey, when did you say the results
of your medical checkup would be ready?

00:07:30.221 --> 00:07:31.514
Next week, I think.

00:07:31.598 --> 00:07:33.767
I'll make a doctor's appointment
and come with you.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.769
It's better if I hear it myself.

00:07:35.852 --> 00:07:38.229
There's no need.
I'm sure nothing's wrong with me.

00:07:38.313 --> 00:07:39.355
Just humor me.

00:07:39.439 --> 00:07:42.233
You don't want to neglect your health
and cost us a fortune later.

00:07:42.317 --> 00:07:45.070
Here. Have some of this too.

00:07:45.153 --> 00:07:47.781
And let's cancel
some of our insurance as well.

00:07:47.864 --> 00:07:50.825
We need to cut our fixed expenses
as much as we can.

00:07:50.909 --> 00:07:55.080
Su-gyeom, you should look into
student loans just in case.

00:07:55.163 --> 00:07:56.081
Okay.

00:07:56.164 --> 00:07:59.542
What's this about loans?
I'll take care of his tuition.

00:07:59.626 --> 00:08:00.960
Gosh.

00:08:01.961 --> 00:08:04.297
Honey, I have to get ready now.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.841
-You didn't even finish your food.
-Oh my.

00:08:07.842 --> 00:08:10.428
Honey, when we go to the campsite later,

00:08:10.512 --> 00:08:11.888
wear this, okay?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.475
And shave your beard

00:08:15.558 --> 00:08:17.310
-so you look clean.
-All right.

00:08:25.527 --> 00:08:26.694
Dad.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.279
Yes?

00:08:28.363 --> 00:08:29.489
Well…

00:08:34.119 --> 00:08:35.912
Is this about
what we discussed?

00:08:37.413 --> 00:08:39.541
Just give me some time. I'm working on it.

00:08:39.624 --> 00:08:41.668
No, I'd been meaning to tell you this.

00:08:43.711 --> 00:08:45.296
They caught the guy who scammed me.

00:08:46.631 --> 00:08:47.674
-Really?
-Yes.

00:08:47.757 --> 00:08:49.092
You don't have to worry anymore.

00:08:51.052 --> 00:08:53.012
Dad, I'm heading out now.

00:08:53.096 --> 00:08:54.597
Why? We can go together.

00:08:54.681 --> 00:08:55.849
I'm running late.

00:08:56.349 --> 00:08:57.433
Jeez.

00:08:57.517 --> 00:08:59.519
-Honey, what are you doing? I'm late.
-Okay.

00:08:59.602 --> 00:09:01.104
Bye, Su-gyeom.

00:09:05.525 --> 00:09:07.777
This is already my fourth interview.

00:09:08.695 --> 00:09:10.822
Some kid way younger than me said,

00:09:11.447 --> 00:09:14.075
"Why should I hire you, Ms. Park Ha-jin?"

00:09:14.742 --> 00:09:17.954
That just completely
crushed my confidence.

00:09:18.997 --> 00:09:22.709
That's why I told you not to waste time
on the real estate license thing.

00:09:22.792 --> 00:09:25.253
You don't have to put up
with that kind of nonsense.

00:09:25.336 --> 00:09:29.007
You think I like hearing that?
I'm doing it so we can make a living.

00:09:32.719 --> 00:09:34.554
Gosh, forget it.

00:09:35.054 --> 00:09:37.640
Hey, don't be late to the campsite.

00:09:37.724 --> 00:09:39.184
Ha-yeong said it was tough to book.

00:09:42.353 --> 00:09:44.355
Do I really have to go?

00:09:44.439 --> 00:09:45.523
Of course you do.

00:09:45.607 --> 00:09:48.109
I arranged this whole thing for you.

00:09:48.193 --> 00:09:51.237
Just come and hear
what Sang-cheol has to say, okay?

00:09:51.946 --> 00:09:53.364
I'm not grilling the meat.

00:09:53.448 --> 00:09:55.742
Fine. I'll grill the meat.

00:09:57.493 --> 00:09:58.786
That's the place, right?

00:10:01.831 --> 00:10:03.249
-Good luck.
-See you later.

00:10:03.333 --> 00:10:04.334
-Okay.
-All right.

00:10:10.673 --> 00:10:12.634
DAHAN REAL ESTATE

00:10:12.717 --> 00:10:13.718
Hello.

00:10:16.137 --> 00:10:17.430
FRIENDLY ADVICE, HONEST SERVICE

00:10:17.513 --> 00:10:18.973
-Please, have a seat.
-Okay.

00:10:20.016 --> 00:10:21.017
Jeez.

00:10:30.777 --> 00:10:31.903
TAKE ONLY WHAT YOU CAN EAT

00:10:32.028 --> 00:10:33.905
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:10:34.822 --> 00:10:35.823
Hello.

00:10:36.407 --> 00:10:37.367
-Hi.
-Hello.

00:10:37.951 --> 00:10:39.535
-Su-gyeom, you're here.
-Hello.

00:10:39.619 --> 00:10:40.662
-Go get ready.
-Okay.

00:10:52.632 --> 00:10:53.758
I'll put these over here.

00:10:53.841 --> 00:10:54.968
Okay.

00:10:57.971 --> 00:10:59.806
Su-gyeom, finish up quickly and go.

00:10:59.889 --> 00:11:01.057
Okay. Bye.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.016
Bye.

00:11:21.035 --> 00:11:23.204
Is this the business
you wanted us to start?

00:11:23.913 --> 00:11:25.039
I have to go back in.

00:11:25.123 --> 00:11:28.042
We proved that we're capable of something.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.795
I get that you don't want
to rely on your dad--

00:11:30.878 --> 00:11:33.881
He offered to give me money.
I was the one who refused it.

00:11:34.716 --> 00:11:35.591
Why?

00:11:35.675 --> 00:11:36.718
Just because.

00:11:38.803 --> 00:11:40.763
If he's offering, why not just take it?

00:11:40.847 --> 00:11:43.016
You can pay him back later.

00:11:43.099 --> 00:11:44.934
What's the big deal?

00:11:47.812 --> 00:11:48.771
Hey.

00:11:49.939 --> 00:11:51.357
What did my dad do wrong?

00:11:52.275 --> 00:11:53.151
What?

00:11:53.234 --> 00:11:55.194
Why should my dad be the one to fund us?

00:11:55.278 --> 00:11:56.404
You could…

00:11:58.072 --> 00:12:00.450
You could ask your parents for help.

00:12:02.869 --> 00:12:04.454
Did I ask him to fund us?

00:12:05.121 --> 00:12:07.457
Did I ask you
to borrow money from your dad?

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.625
No, but what's with your attitude?

00:12:10.168 --> 00:12:12.545
Who do you think got me into this mess?

00:12:16.716 --> 00:12:17.884
So it's my fault again?

00:12:18.801 --> 00:12:22.096
Are you saying it's my fault
for introducing you to Lee Jeong-hwan?

00:12:27.477 --> 00:12:28.436
Fine.

00:12:29.854 --> 00:12:31.356
Give me your account number.

00:12:31.939 --> 00:12:35.443
I'll pay off your 30 million won,
so just type in your account number.

00:12:39.364 --> 00:12:42.617
Here, take this for now.

00:12:43.242 --> 00:12:44.410
I'll send you the rest later.

00:12:44.494 --> 00:12:46.162
-Han-na.
-I've given it some thought.

00:12:46.245 --> 00:12:47.455
I'm going back to the US.

00:12:47.538 --> 00:12:50.208
We shouldn't have let things between us

00:12:50.291 --> 00:12:52.502
become more
than fond middle school memories.

00:12:55.004 --> 00:12:56.172
I'm sorry, Su-gyeom.

00:12:57.298 --> 00:12:58.674
I ruined everything.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.344
I'll talk to my parents
as soon as I get there

00:13:01.427 --> 00:13:02.512
and send the money.

00:13:02.595 --> 00:13:04.889
It won't take long. Take care.

00:13:20.905 --> 00:13:22.573
I thought we would be
grilling our own meat.

00:13:22.657 --> 00:13:24.742
No,
they do everything for you here.

00:13:26.035 --> 00:13:27.036
Thank you.

00:13:27.662 --> 00:13:30.331
This isn't the kind of camping
we had in mind.

00:13:30.415 --> 00:13:32.542
-I know.
-We should've brought Su-gyeom.

00:13:32.625 --> 00:13:34.502
-Please have a lovely time.
-Thank you.

00:13:37.588 --> 00:13:39.006
Nak-su, you've worked so hard.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:39.966
Oh, please.

00:13:40.049 --> 00:13:43.636
I wish you the best of health
in the next chapter of your life.

00:13:43.719 --> 00:13:45.471
Congratulations, Nak-su.

00:13:45.555 --> 00:13:47.890
-I hope your business is a success.
-Thank you.

00:13:48.766 --> 00:13:51.519
But why did you quit your job?

00:13:54.313 --> 00:13:55.440
It wasn't any fun.

00:13:55.523 --> 00:13:58.359
And I figured I'd try something new.

00:13:58.443 --> 00:14:02.029
He's already received so many offers.

00:14:02.113 --> 00:14:03.489
I bet.

00:14:03.573 --> 00:14:06.200
He worked at such a huge company
for 25 years, after all.

00:14:08.202 --> 00:14:11.289
I recently had to find a sales director,

00:14:11.372 --> 00:14:12.623
but it was quite a struggle.

00:14:12.707 --> 00:14:14.542
Since you were the standard,

00:14:14.625 --> 00:14:16.294
no one quite measured up to you.

00:14:18.087 --> 00:14:19.464
Really?

00:14:22.717 --> 00:14:26.262
Well, you need to hire people
if you're going to start a business.

00:14:26.345 --> 00:14:28.347
So what will you be doing now?

00:14:28.431 --> 00:14:29.765
Do you have any plans?

00:14:29.849 --> 00:14:31.809
I bet the severance pay wasn't much.

00:14:33.644 --> 00:14:35.021
It's more than you'd think.

00:14:37.315 --> 00:14:39.692
Goodness, you worry about everything.

00:14:39.775 --> 00:14:42.195
I'm sure Nak-su has a plan. Right?

00:14:42.278 --> 00:14:43.613
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:14:43.696 --> 00:14:46.199
So I want to know what the plan is.
What is it?

00:14:47.909 --> 00:14:49.118
Where's the restroom?

00:14:49.202 --> 00:14:51.287
Over there. Let me come with you.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.080
-This way.
-Eat up.

00:14:53.164 --> 00:14:54.916
I'll be right back.

00:14:54.999 --> 00:14:56.834
-This way, Nak-su.
-Okay, thanks.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:06.469
My wife told me
you wanted to make me an offer.

00:15:08.596 --> 00:15:09.722
I did.

00:15:10.765 --> 00:15:14.352
I guess it wasn't
the right time for me back then.

00:15:15.686 --> 00:15:17.563
Are you interested now?

00:15:18.231 --> 00:15:21.776
Didn't you say you already hired someone?

00:15:21.859 --> 00:15:24.612
You can never have too many sales people.

00:15:25.238 --> 00:15:27.031
Really?

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.625
But if you decide to join us,

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:42.046
you might have to work
under someone who joined before you.

00:15:42.797 --> 00:15:43.673
And?

00:15:43.756 --> 00:15:46.092
In that case,
I may not be able to match the terms

00:15:46.175 --> 00:15:47.969
that I originally had in mind.

00:15:48.052 --> 00:15:49.971
What, are you going to offer me
two million won?

00:15:50.054 --> 00:15:53.182
Goodness, Nak-su. Of course not.

00:15:53.266 --> 00:15:55.017
Why not? Two million sounds fine.

00:15:55.101 --> 00:15:59.313
I'd have to offer you
at least 2.2 or 2.3 million won.

00:15:59.397 --> 00:16:02.858
Nak-su. I really want you in my company.

00:16:04.151 --> 00:16:05.278
Just a second.

00:16:05.861 --> 00:16:06.862
Hi, Mr. Eom.

00:16:06.946 --> 00:16:07.905
Yes, I can talk.

00:16:07.989 --> 00:16:09.323
I'll see you in a bit.

00:16:11.158 --> 00:16:12.535
Yes, I saw that.

00:16:12.618 --> 00:16:14.120
What do the investors keep asking for?

00:16:14.203 --> 00:16:15.413
The IR and what else?

00:16:16.497 --> 00:16:18.124
That son of a…

00:16:20.418 --> 00:16:21.294
Hey.

00:16:23.421 --> 00:16:25.590
-By any chance--
-Wait. Let me go first.

00:16:26.215 --> 00:16:27.800
I'm saying this just in case.

00:16:27.883 --> 00:16:30.386
There's not an opening
at his company anymore.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.472
I don't want you to get your hopes up.

00:16:34.223 --> 00:16:37.893
The offer was months ago.
Nak-su said he wasn't interested.

00:16:38.561 --> 00:16:40.021
That ship has sailed.

00:16:43.899 --> 00:16:47.236
Don't tell me
that's why you wanted to meet today.

00:16:47.862 --> 00:16:49.238
No, of course not.

00:16:49.322 --> 00:16:51.574
Of course not, right?

00:16:51.657 --> 00:16:53.326
I was almost disappointed.

00:16:54.035 --> 00:16:58.372
The high and mighty Park Ha-jin

00:16:58.456 --> 00:17:01.542
wouldn't possibly be asking
for a job for her husband.

00:17:01.626 --> 00:17:03.419
No way.

00:17:04.086 --> 00:17:06.297
-Hey!
-Come to think of it.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.134
I think they said they needed

00:17:10.217 --> 00:17:14.764
another person to work under the director.

00:17:30.446 --> 00:17:32.490
For the first time ever,

00:17:33.199 --> 00:17:36.702
I feel like I have you
in the palm of my hand.

00:17:38.579 --> 00:17:40.039
-Do you, now?
-Yes.

00:17:40.915 --> 00:17:43.626
My sister, who has nagged me
like my mom my whole life,

00:17:43.709 --> 00:17:48.089
is now groveling before me
over her husband's job.

00:17:51.967 --> 00:17:53.135
Hey,

00:17:53.219 --> 00:17:54.553
is Sang-cheol not back yet?

00:17:54.637 --> 00:17:55.680
He left first.

00:17:56.222 --> 00:17:58.432
Nak-su! Be good to my sister.

00:17:58.516 --> 00:17:59.725
I already am.

00:18:00.518 --> 00:18:03.145
My sister really loves you.

00:18:03.688 --> 00:18:06.315
-Okay.
-All right. We'll do that.

00:18:06.399 --> 00:18:08.776
Great. Talk to you soon.

00:18:10.027 --> 00:18:11.404
Who were you talking to?

00:18:11.487 --> 00:18:13.114
Mr. Eom.

00:18:14.865 --> 00:18:16.659
The guy you hired instead of Nak-su?

00:18:16.742 --> 00:18:17.743
Yes.

00:18:22.331 --> 00:18:25.251
So is there an opening for him or not?

00:18:25.334 --> 00:18:28.504
Gosh,
I really want him to join us.

00:18:29.797 --> 00:18:33.384
Please consider what I told you.

00:18:38.305 --> 00:18:40.224
What a supportive wife.

00:18:40.307 --> 00:18:41.434
What was that?

00:18:41.517 --> 00:18:42.893
Nothing.

00:19:07.084 --> 00:19:10.546
My dearest, happy Ha-yeong.

00:19:14.175 --> 00:19:16.510
Please think it over.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.681
I promise I'll stop nagging you like Mom

00:19:20.765 --> 00:19:22.892
and be good to you, okay?

00:19:24.935 --> 00:19:26.020
I'm counting on you.

00:19:26.896 --> 00:19:27.855
Okay.

00:19:30.733 --> 00:19:32.735
-You've had enough.
-All right.

00:19:42.536 --> 00:19:43.913
Are you okay?

00:19:45.998 --> 00:19:48.918
What about you? Are you okay?

00:19:50.294 --> 00:19:52.421
Yes, I am. Why wouldn't I be?

00:19:53.214 --> 00:19:54.673
Then I'm okay too.

00:20:09.688 --> 00:20:11.148
SOL E&TECH
CEO CHO YUN-HYEONG

00:20:11.774 --> 00:20:14.318
Did the managing director of sales quit?

00:20:15.319 --> 00:20:17.571
I'll be in touch. Bye.

00:20:17.655 --> 00:20:19.448
Not that it matters,

00:20:20.157 --> 00:20:23.160
but didn't you say that one director quit?

00:20:23.953 --> 00:20:25.955
Damn, this is tough.

00:20:26.038 --> 00:20:27.373
SOL E&TECH CEO CHO YUN-HYEONG

00:20:27.498 --> 00:20:31.377
You talked smack about them
because they were so bad at their job.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.462
You're my favorite person
to drink with too.

00:20:33.546 --> 00:20:34.505
When should we meet?

00:20:34.588 --> 00:20:38.050
How about I come over and give you
some pointers on the art of sales?

00:20:38.133 --> 00:20:40.386
Sounds good. And the timing's perfect.

00:20:40.886 --> 00:20:43.514
I'm thinking of opening a new branch.

00:20:43.597 --> 00:20:46.308
And I'd feel a lot better
if someone like you could take charge.

00:20:46.392 --> 00:20:48.644
A new branch? Where?

00:20:49.562 --> 00:20:50.437
CEO KIM RYUN-HOE

00:20:50.521 --> 00:20:51.522
In Jamsil.

00:20:51.605 --> 00:20:55.276
I'm thinking of a one-stop shop
for everything from demos to sales.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:59.822
That's definitely the trend
in retail these days.

00:20:59.905 --> 00:21:01.991
You sure know
what you're doing.

00:21:02.074 --> 00:21:04.535
If you're going to keep talking
like you're better than me,

00:21:04.618 --> 00:21:05.744
we're done here.

00:21:10.374 --> 00:21:11.542
Please continue, sir.

00:21:13.377 --> 00:21:17.423
The base pay is two big ones a month,
and you can earn more through incentives.

00:21:18.716 --> 00:21:20.301
Two big ones?

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.595
Not 20 million.

00:21:25.431 --> 00:21:26.348
CEO JANG MIN-GYU

00:21:26.432 --> 00:21:28.017
I can't go higher than two million.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:29.351
Two-point-two million won.

00:21:30.102 --> 00:21:31.353
Before taxes.

00:21:31.437 --> 00:21:33.772
-We can't afford to hire anyone right now.
-I see.

00:21:33.856 --> 00:21:35.858
I see you were born in 1972.

00:21:35.941 --> 00:21:37.318
-You entered college in '91?
-Yes.

00:21:37.401 --> 00:21:38.277
I see.

00:21:39.987 --> 00:21:42.031
Our CEO was born in 1976.

00:21:42.114 --> 00:21:44.116
Sales! So important.

00:21:44.199 --> 00:21:47.202
That's why I do it all at my company.

00:21:47.828 --> 00:21:50.289
Wow, you're even available
to work on weekends?

00:21:50.372 --> 00:21:52.625
-Yes.
-Awesome!

00:21:52.708 --> 00:21:54.084
In that case…

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:56.045
Two million.

00:21:59.131 --> 00:22:02.217
Isn't base pay for sales always low?
It's all about the incentives.

00:22:02.301 --> 00:22:04.053
But still, man!

00:22:04.136 --> 00:22:05.971
Until last week, I was a general manager.

00:22:06.055 --> 00:22:08.015
I can't work for that kind of money.

00:22:09.099 --> 00:22:11.769
Even delivery drivers
make five million a month.

00:22:11.852 --> 00:22:12.853
Then do that.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.022
I can't drive a truck.

00:22:16.732 --> 00:22:17.691
Right. That's true.

00:22:18.233 --> 00:22:21.070
Then you'll just have to live
off your severance pay.

00:22:21.153 --> 00:22:22.571
Come on.

00:22:27.493 --> 00:22:29.328
So, what have you been up to?

00:22:29.411 --> 00:22:30.329
What do you mean?

00:22:30.412 --> 00:22:31.872
What's your daily routine?

00:22:33.332 --> 00:22:36.210
Well, once I get up in the morning,

00:22:36.293 --> 00:22:39.338
I work out, come home, wash up,

00:22:39.421 --> 00:22:42.132
read the paper for a bit,
and eat with my wife.

00:22:42.216 --> 00:22:43.092
Jeez.

00:22:43.175 --> 00:22:44.802
We eat out from time to time,

00:22:44.885 --> 00:22:46.887
and on the way back,
I check on my building.

00:22:46.971 --> 00:22:48.138
And sometimes I go hiking.

00:22:48.222 --> 00:22:49.640
That's pretty much it.

00:22:49.723 --> 00:22:52.768
Must be nice. Life is certainly different
on 30 million a month.

00:22:52.851 --> 00:22:55.729
Did I not tell you? It's 32 million now.

00:22:55.813 --> 00:22:58.190
I get a share from the cafe, you see.

00:23:02.111 --> 00:23:03.404
32 MILLION WON / MONTH

00:23:04.154 --> 00:23:06.281
I'm so damn jealous of you, Mr. Landlord.

00:23:11.286 --> 00:23:12.246
Don't do it.

00:23:12.913 --> 00:23:15.416
-Don't do what?
-Whatever it is.

00:23:15.499 --> 00:23:18.127
Don't even think about doing
what you're planning right now.

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:19.169
Stop right there.

00:23:20.504 --> 00:23:22.506
Don't you dare touch your severance pay.

00:23:22.589 --> 00:23:23.924
Just leave it be.

00:23:24.008 --> 00:23:26.343
If you do something
you're not cut out for,

00:23:26.427 --> 00:23:28.262
it'll only come back to bite you.

00:23:28.345 --> 00:23:30.305
Just focus on finding a job.

00:23:30.389 --> 00:23:32.474
You're cut out for the corporate life.

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.815
NTC CARD PAYMENT COMPLETE: 1,687,150 WON

00:23:39.898 --> 00:23:41.775
Jeez, another credit card bill.

00:23:41.859 --> 00:23:44.278
You can't think the same way you did
when you had a job.

00:23:44.361 --> 00:23:46.196
You have to cut down on your spending.

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.282
Hey, I'll pay for everything today,

00:23:48.907 --> 00:23:50.993
so listen to me nag a bit more.

00:23:51.076 --> 00:23:53.746
Canned peaches, smoked drumsticks,
and spicy jerky, right?

00:23:54.455 --> 00:23:55.581
Thanks, Mr. Landlord.

00:23:55.664 --> 00:23:57.416
And some anchovies too.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.752
Man, you've got quite the appetite.

00:24:05.466 --> 00:24:06.884
Thanks, take care.

00:24:09.928 --> 00:24:11.055
DELIVERY DRIVER WANTED

00:24:11.764 --> 00:24:15.017
A delivery driver makes five million.

00:24:17.519 --> 00:24:19.563
A courier makes three and a half million.

00:24:23.317 --> 00:24:26.612
A designated driver
makes about four million.

00:24:28.947 --> 00:24:33.035
A retiree on a pension
gets about six million.

00:24:33.994 --> 00:24:36.747
A golf instructor makes seven million.

00:24:38.248 --> 00:24:42.044
Six million, seven million, six--

00:24:42.127 --> 00:24:43.253
Hello, gentlemen.

00:24:43.337 --> 00:24:45.881
We want to tell you about
a great commercial building.

00:24:45.964 --> 00:24:47.508
SALARY ENDS
BUT RENT DOESN'T

00:24:48.967 --> 00:24:50.260
If you invest now,

00:24:50.344 --> 00:24:53.555
you'll be able to collect
about six to seven million won in rent.

00:24:58.519 --> 00:25:00.270
Hey, I need to go home. I'll call you.

00:25:00.354 --> 00:25:02.356
-Sorry.
-Hey, Nak-su!

00:25:02.439 --> 00:25:03.524
Where are you going?

00:25:04.024 --> 00:25:05.192
Hey!

00:25:33.095 --> 00:25:35.514
SALARY ENDS
BUT RENT DOESN'T

00:25:39.726 --> 00:25:42.312
Yes, we're still selling
units in our building.

00:25:42.396 --> 00:25:44.648
But you might want to hurry.

00:25:44.731 --> 00:25:46.817
We're almost out of units.

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:48.068
Take a brochure.

00:25:48.152 --> 00:25:49.444
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:25:50.028 --> 00:25:51.697
Please take a fan.

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:53.490
Please come in for a consultation.

00:25:54.158 --> 00:25:55.659
Did you know?

00:25:55.742 --> 00:25:56.827
Salary ends…

00:25:56.910 --> 00:25:59.079
-…but rent doesn't!
-…but rent doesn't!

00:25:59.163 --> 00:26:00.789
-Come take a look inside.
-Thank you.

00:26:00.873 --> 00:26:02.374
-Thank you.
-Please go on in.

00:26:02.457 --> 00:26:03.876
Yes, you can go in now.

00:26:03.959 --> 00:26:04.877
SHOWROOM
UNITS FOR SALE

00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:06.670
-Come take a look.
-Feel free to look around.

00:26:06.753 --> 00:26:08.255
Hello, please take a fan.

00:26:08.338 --> 00:26:10.465
I look forward to working with you too.

00:26:10.549 --> 00:26:14.011
Hello, welcome to AP Royal.
Do you have an appointment?

00:26:14.094 --> 00:26:15.637
No, I just came to take a look.

00:26:15.721 --> 00:26:17.055
Welcome, sir.

00:26:18.223 --> 00:26:20.684
-Did you call to make an appointment?
-No, I didn't.

00:26:20.767 --> 00:26:23.353
I'm sorry. All our consultation slots
are fully booked for the day.

00:26:23.437 --> 00:26:25.355
How long until the next appointment?

00:26:25.439 --> 00:26:26.815
About 15 minutes?

00:26:26.899 --> 00:26:30.194
Sir, I'm afraid
I only have about 15 minutes.

00:26:30.277 --> 00:26:32.446
-Would that still be okay?
-Sure, that's fine.

00:26:33.947 --> 00:26:34.948
Please come this way.

00:26:39.077 --> 00:26:40.829
MANGJIN PLAZA SALES GALLERY

00:26:46.043 --> 00:26:47.878
To drink, we have coffee, green tea,

00:26:47.961 --> 00:26:50.714
ssanghwatang, and Job's tears tea.
What can I get for you?

00:26:50.797 --> 00:26:52.424
I'll just have a hot coffee, please.

00:26:52.507 --> 00:26:54.009
One hot coffee.

00:26:54.092 --> 00:26:55.052
Okay.

00:26:56.762 --> 00:26:59.473
So what brings you here today?

00:27:00.474 --> 00:27:02.017
You really don't remember me, do you?

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:04.478
You gave me a flyer
at the convenience store.

00:27:05.479 --> 00:27:08.106
Yes, of course. I think I remember now.

00:27:08.190 --> 00:27:09.858
This must be fate.

00:27:10.525 --> 00:27:11.902
So, have you sold any?

00:27:12.444 --> 00:27:14.446
It looks like these are all sold already.

00:27:14.529 --> 00:27:15.948
You're quite late, sir.

00:27:16.031 --> 00:27:19.743
Well, there's only one property left
that's worth showing you.

00:27:20.494 --> 00:27:22.371
It's definitely a great unit.

00:27:22.454 --> 00:27:25.958
It's a bit pricey,
so I'm a little hesitant to bring it up.

00:27:26.041 --> 00:27:28.126
Let's hear it.
You said you didn't have much time.

00:27:28.210 --> 00:27:31.004
All right, then let me give you
a quick rundown.

00:27:31.088 --> 00:27:32.130
MANGJIN PLAZA

00:27:32.214 --> 00:27:35.217
First off, the building is located
in a well-connected area.

00:27:35.300 --> 00:27:38.845
Let's skip that part.
I saw the news about the Line 5 extension.

00:27:38.929 --> 00:27:40.472
Then let me just tell you this.

00:27:40.555 --> 00:27:44.017
I walked from the station
to the building myself yesterday.

00:27:44.101 --> 00:27:46.520
We've been advertising it
as a five-minute walk.

00:27:46.603 --> 00:27:49.106
But guess what?
It was a three-minute walk.

00:27:49.189 --> 00:27:52.192
Salespeople always say
something is close to the station.

00:27:52.276 --> 00:27:54.236
It really was a three-minute walk.

00:27:54.319 --> 00:27:56.863
That doesn't mean anything.
You need a lot of foot traffic.

00:27:56.947 --> 00:27:59.992
And there will be
a lot of demand in the area.

00:28:00.075 --> 00:28:03.245
As you can see, a major IT company
is building its new HQ nearby.

00:28:03.328 --> 00:28:04.663
It's just been approved.

00:28:04.746 --> 00:28:07.124
The nearby 50,000-home
residential district is nearly full.

00:28:07.207 --> 00:28:08.875
And there are schools nearby too.

00:28:10.335 --> 00:28:11.461
So in my opinion,

00:28:11.545 --> 00:28:13.630
the quality and quantity
of foot traffic here

00:28:14.256 --> 00:28:15.716
is nearly on par with Gangnam Station.

00:28:15.799 --> 00:28:18.385
Gangnam Station? That's ridiculous.

00:28:18.468 --> 00:28:20.053
-Sir.
-Yes.

00:28:20.137 --> 00:28:21.722
I'm the expert here.

00:28:22.389 --> 00:28:25.976
This location is one of the best
I've seen in my entire career.

00:28:26.059 --> 00:28:28.645
Still, comparing it to Gangnam Station…

00:28:29.146 --> 00:28:30.022
Thank you.

00:28:30.105 --> 00:28:31.690
-Here's your coffee.
-Thanks.

00:28:31.773 --> 00:28:34.318
So it's in a prime school district.

00:28:35.360 --> 00:28:37.029
What kind of businesses
have moved in here?

00:28:37.112 --> 00:28:38.822
Let's see. On the first floor,

00:28:38.905 --> 00:28:41.074
a franchise restaurant
and a big pharmacy have signed on.

00:28:41.158 --> 00:28:44.619
Clinics are on floors two to five. Dental,
psychiatry, pediatrics, and dermatology.

00:28:44.703 --> 00:28:46.413
Interior work will begin soon.

00:28:47.080 --> 00:28:48.081
The basement is empty.

00:28:48.165 --> 00:28:49.708
In the basement, a famous influencer

00:28:49.791 --> 00:28:52.502
is opening a large indoor
golf simulator facility.

00:28:53.628 --> 00:28:56.757
Now, if you look at the overall layout,

00:28:56.840 --> 00:28:58.216
one type of business is missing.

00:28:58.300 --> 00:28:59.718
What do you think it is?

00:28:59.801 --> 00:29:02.679
Well…

00:29:02.763 --> 00:29:05.265
Sir, let me give you a hint.

00:29:05.349 --> 00:29:06.641
-Okay.
-Right here.

00:29:06.725 --> 00:29:07.684
FRANCHISE RESTAURANT

00:29:07.768 --> 00:29:10.771
After you have a meal
at the restaurant and come outside…

00:29:10.854 --> 00:29:11.772
Oh, coffee.

00:29:11.855 --> 00:29:14.816
-There's no cafe here.
-You've got sharp eyes, sir.

00:29:14.900 --> 00:29:17.569
Five franchise cafes
are in talks with us right now.

00:29:18.111 --> 00:29:20.280
They all think it's a must-have location.

00:29:20.364 --> 00:29:21.239
Which ones are they?

00:29:22.032 --> 00:29:24.868
The bidding is too competitive
for me to disclose that.

00:29:27.412 --> 00:29:28.914
Is this one of them?

00:29:33.001 --> 00:29:34.378
Keep this to yourself.

00:29:35.003 --> 00:29:37.089
They're the most likely candidate.

00:29:37.714 --> 00:29:39.758
They never miss out on a prime location.

00:29:39.841 --> 00:29:42.844
Their market analysis
is incredibly thorough.

00:29:43.720 --> 00:29:47.140
Well, major corporations
are always meticulous.

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:53.105
By any chance, you…

00:29:56.024 --> 00:29:57.025
I actually

00:29:57.943 --> 00:29:59.820
worked at ACT for about 25 years.

00:29:59.903 --> 00:30:01.780
I just retired.

00:30:01.863 --> 00:30:03.365
That explains it.

00:30:03.448 --> 00:30:05.992
You have the air of
a big company executive.

00:30:06.076 --> 00:30:08.829
I got tired of it and quit.

00:30:08.912 --> 00:30:10.122
So, where's this unit?

00:30:10.205 --> 00:30:12.958
If you look here, it's in the corner.

00:30:13.041 --> 00:30:14.084
It's the only one left.

00:30:14.793 --> 00:30:16.211
I knew that would be the one.

00:30:16.294 --> 00:30:18.672
I had my eye on that spot from the start.

00:30:18.755 --> 00:30:22.050
A corner spot like this
gets traffic from both sides.

00:30:22.134 --> 00:30:23.176
My goodness.

00:30:23.260 --> 00:30:25.137
How do you know so much about this?

00:30:25.220 --> 00:30:26.096
Oh, please.

00:30:26.763 --> 00:30:30.684
With a spot like that, the monthly income
from rent would be about six…

00:30:32.394 --> 00:30:33.854
Maybe seven…

00:30:37.649 --> 00:30:39.151
It would be about nine million.

00:30:40.110 --> 00:30:40.986
I see.

00:30:42.112 --> 00:30:43.655
I bet you already knew that.

00:30:43.738 --> 00:30:46.158
No, I thought
it'd be around eight million.

00:30:46.241 --> 00:30:48.660
I see. Nine million…

00:30:48.743 --> 00:30:50.829
Yes, this row here is eight million.

00:30:50.912 --> 00:30:52.456
So this one gets nine million, no less.

00:30:52.539 --> 00:30:54.082
-I see.
-Yes.

00:30:54.166 --> 00:30:56.126
But with VAT, it's about 9.9 million.

00:30:56.209 --> 00:30:59.546
You can think of it as ten a month.

00:31:01.173 --> 00:31:02.048
Ten million a month?

00:31:03.133 --> 00:31:04.509
Ten million a month.

00:31:04.593 --> 00:31:06.720
Ten million, ten million a month.

00:31:06.803 --> 00:31:08.305
Ten million a month.

00:31:08.388 --> 00:31:11.016
10 MILLION WON / MONTH

00:31:11.099 --> 00:31:13.768
All right. Ten million a month.

00:31:13.852 --> 00:31:16.021
-What's the price then?
-It's 1.6 billion won.

00:31:16.104 --> 00:31:18.273
-What?
-It's 1.6 billion.

00:31:19.191 --> 00:31:21.860
Jeez. That's way too expensive.

00:31:21.943 --> 00:31:23.069
-Sir.
-Yes?

00:31:23.153 --> 00:31:25.614
Finding tenants is key
for commercial buildings.

00:31:25.697 --> 00:31:28.992
And it's impossible for this spot
to ever be vacant.

00:31:29.075 --> 00:31:29.993
A solid investment.

00:31:30.076 --> 00:31:31.661
I know that.

00:31:31.745 --> 00:31:35.123
But 1.6 billion flat, with no discount?

00:31:35.207 --> 00:31:36.124
Come on.

00:31:36.791 --> 00:31:39.878
As I mentioned earlier,
you're really quite late to the game.

00:31:40.504 --> 00:31:43.048
Even the promotions
we were running before have all ended,

00:31:43.131 --> 00:31:45.634
so it's hard to give you a discount.
I'm sorry.

00:31:49.054 --> 00:31:52.432
Well, it's a shame,
but I guess that's that.

00:31:52.516 --> 00:31:53.642
-I should--
-Sir.

00:31:53.725 --> 00:31:55.185
Are you interested at all?

00:31:55.268 --> 00:31:58.563
My interest would depend on how you--

00:31:58.647 --> 00:32:00.190
-Sir!
-Why are you grabbing--

00:32:00.273 --> 00:32:01.483
Please sit for a moment.

00:32:01.566 --> 00:32:04.027
Didn't you say you didn't have time?

00:32:04.110 --> 00:32:05.820
-Please, just a second.
-Goodness.

00:32:05.904 --> 00:32:07.447
Gosh. Seriously.

00:32:07.531 --> 00:32:09.199
You really drive a hard bargain.

00:32:10.867 --> 00:32:12.869
All right. Then I'll…

00:32:16.915 --> 00:32:18.458
Let me ask my director.

00:32:18.542 --> 00:32:20.210
What's there to ask?

00:32:20.919 --> 00:32:22.671
I bet you've got no say in this.

00:32:22.754 --> 00:32:23.755
It's nothing.

00:32:23.838 --> 00:32:25.131
He has sharp hearing.

00:32:31.763 --> 00:32:33.598
This electrifying tension.

00:32:34.266 --> 00:32:36.059
This gambler's instinct.

00:32:36.560 --> 00:32:38.520
Ten-million-a-month Nak-su!

00:32:42.941 --> 00:32:44.442
You can start next week.

00:32:46.403 --> 00:32:47.320
Really?

00:32:47.404 --> 00:32:50.490
You were a top credit card salesperson.
How could we not hire you?

00:32:51.783 --> 00:32:53.243
Show us what you've got.

00:32:53.326 --> 00:32:54.661
Yes, of course.

00:32:55.620 --> 00:32:58.164
I'll do my absolute best.

00:33:01.626 --> 00:33:03.545
Oh my.

00:33:04.170 --> 00:33:06.006
There's no need to cry.

00:33:06.089 --> 00:33:08.550
I just thought of my husband.

00:33:14.306 --> 00:33:16.891
Where is he?

00:33:21.271 --> 00:33:23.106
Come on, Kim Nak-su.

00:33:23.189 --> 00:33:25.525
Pick up the phone!
Why aren't you answering?

00:33:26.818 --> 00:33:28.903
HA-JIN

00:33:36.202 --> 00:33:37.370
Just a moment.

00:33:43.585 --> 00:33:46.004
This is the pre-construction price
from a year ago.

00:33:46.087 --> 00:33:48.173
I told the director
that you're a former ACT executive,

00:33:48.256 --> 00:33:51.426
and he said, "Goodness,
we're no match for him."

00:33:51.509 --> 00:33:53.720
So he gave you
such a generous discount right away.

00:33:53.803 --> 00:33:55.722
I was honestly shocked when I heard.

00:33:56.264 --> 00:34:00.226
So, 1.1 billion won?
That's the price of a decent apartment.

00:34:00.310 --> 00:34:03.521
And to sink all that into a unit
in a commercial building?

00:34:06.399 --> 00:34:08.234
Sir.

00:34:08.318 --> 00:34:10.779
-Oh, dear. Is it time already?
-Are you leaving?

00:34:10.862 --> 00:34:12.781
Just give me five more minutes.

00:34:12.864 --> 00:34:14.366
Just five minutes.

00:34:14.449 --> 00:34:15.825
Five minutes.

00:34:16.534 --> 00:34:19.454
Sir, what if we think about it this way?

00:34:19.537 --> 00:34:21.247
-How should we think about it?
-There are…

00:34:21.331 --> 00:34:23.166
-Yes.
-…no resale restrictions here.

00:34:23.249 --> 00:34:25.835
You can sell it right away
after you buy it.

00:34:25.919 --> 00:34:27.712
So you buy it for 1.1 billion won.

00:34:27.796 --> 00:34:30.340
Then you put it on the market
for 400 million more.

00:34:30.423 --> 00:34:31.466
It'll sell in a flash.

00:34:31.549 --> 00:34:33.468
You'll make 400 million won
just by sitting back.

00:34:33.551 --> 00:34:37.138
All right. Why are you
getting worked up? Calm down.

00:34:37.222 --> 00:34:38.640
In that case…

00:34:39.349 --> 00:34:41.101
-Knock off 100 million won.
-What?

00:34:41.184 --> 00:34:42.727
-Make it one billion won.
-No way.

00:34:42.811 --> 00:34:44.604
Let's just make it an even one billion.

00:34:44.688 --> 00:34:47.899
There are plenty of people
willing to pay the full 1.6 billion won.

00:34:47.982 --> 00:34:50.694
It's much better for us
to sell it to them.

00:34:50.777 --> 00:34:51.653
Hold on.

00:34:53.613 --> 00:34:56.199
Then just sell it to them for 1.6 billion.

00:34:56.282 --> 00:34:58.993
Why are you selling it to me for less?

00:35:01.663 --> 00:35:04.124
Despite everything, why do you think

00:35:04.207 --> 00:35:06.710
I'm making you such a special offer?

00:35:06.793 --> 00:35:08.461
Why would that be?

00:35:10.630 --> 00:35:12.298
It's because I believe you

00:35:13.883 --> 00:35:16.636
would take good care of this unit.

00:35:19.764 --> 00:35:21.141
Gosh.

00:35:21.683 --> 00:35:23.643
How did you know my job
was in management?

00:35:23.727 --> 00:35:25.729
You're amazing.

00:35:25.812 --> 00:35:28.314
Sir, I've met my fair share of people.

00:35:28.398 --> 00:35:29.899
I could tell just by looking at you.

00:35:29.983 --> 00:35:34.154
"Here's someone who knows
how to get things done."

00:35:34.237 --> 00:35:35.780
Okay, I get it.

00:35:35.864 --> 00:35:38.742
I'll take good care of it.

00:35:38.825 --> 00:35:41.327
So make it one billion won.

00:35:41.411 --> 00:35:42.704
No way. Good lord.

00:35:42.787 --> 00:35:43.913
Please leave. I'm late.

00:35:43.997 --> 00:35:46.040
Come on, I'm sure you all need

00:35:46.124 --> 00:35:48.084
to sell it fast so you can pack up.

00:35:48.168 --> 00:35:50.628
The labor, operating costs,
and the promoters

00:35:50.712 --> 00:35:53.923
would cost you at least
a few million won a day.

00:35:55.717 --> 00:35:59.304
This is why it's such a headache
dealing with seasoned veterans like you.

00:35:59.387 --> 00:36:01.222
You already know everything!

00:36:01.306 --> 00:36:04.434
I can give a quote right away,
just by taking a quick glance.

00:36:04.517 --> 00:36:05.977
It's nothing, really.

00:36:07.020 --> 00:36:08.354
Fine. All right.

00:36:08.438 --> 00:36:09.856
In that case,

00:36:09.939 --> 00:36:11.691
let's do 1.05 billion.

00:36:11.775 --> 00:36:14.486
What's with the 0.05?
Let's just make it an even one billion.

00:36:15.487 --> 00:36:16.946
I can't.

00:36:17.030 --> 00:36:19.324
You should go.
I really can't make that happen.

00:36:19.407 --> 00:36:21.576
Why are you being so dramatic?
We were just talking--

00:36:21.659 --> 00:36:23.912
-What's wrong?
-One moment. I have a call.

00:36:23.995 --> 00:36:25.705
-I ignored mine.
-Yes, sir.

00:36:25.789 --> 00:36:27.248
Let's just--

00:36:27.332 --> 00:36:28.958
-Jeez.
-You're on your way now?

00:36:29.042 --> 00:36:30.084
Yes.

00:36:30.168 --> 00:36:32.670
I was just talking
to someone about that unit.

00:36:32.754 --> 00:36:35.173
-We just wrapped things up.
-What do you mean, "wrapped up"?

00:36:35.256 --> 00:36:37.675
No. I can see you
after my next appointment, sir.

00:36:38.676 --> 00:36:41.179
Okay, I'll see you soon.

00:36:41.262 --> 00:36:42.347
All right. Bye.

00:36:42.430 --> 00:36:44.057
Wait a minute. What?

00:36:44.724 --> 00:36:48.186
Hey, we weren't done talking.
I haven't even made up my mind yet.

00:36:48.269 --> 00:36:50.104
Then please take time to think it over.

00:36:50.188 --> 00:36:51.981
Give me a call when you've decided.

00:36:52.065 --> 00:36:53.900
I'm running late.
It's gonna delay everything.

00:36:53.983 --> 00:36:55.860
Okay. Fine.

00:36:59.864 --> 00:37:00.865
So, you'll take it?

00:37:10.291 --> 00:37:11.543
Come sit down.

00:37:12.377 --> 00:37:13.419
In that case…

00:37:16.422 --> 00:37:17.298
What is it?

00:37:17.382 --> 00:37:19.092
Talk it over with your wife and come back.

00:37:19.175 --> 00:37:21.553
Jeez, why are you
making this so hard for me?

00:37:21.636 --> 00:37:23.054
We feel more comfortable that way.

00:37:23.137 --> 00:37:25.807
It's my money.
Why do I need to talk it over with anyone?

00:37:25.890 --> 00:37:26.766
Get back here.

00:37:27.767 --> 00:37:29.853
-I understand.
-Jeez.

00:37:29.936 --> 00:37:31.229
In that case, sir,

00:37:32.438 --> 00:37:34.399
please wire the deposit now.

00:37:34.941 --> 00:37:36.526
We should put this on hold.

00:37:36.609 --> 00:37:38.820
Or the other buyers
will end up wasting their trip.

00:37:38.903 --> 00:37:40.738
-How much?
-Ten percent of the principal.

00:37:44.409 --> 00:37:47.662
Hold on. I have a favor to ask,
and this is very important.

00:37:47.745 --> 00:37:49.747
You absolutely can't tell any other owners

00:37:49.831 --> 00:37:52.166
that you got a 550 million won discount.

00:37:52.250 --> 00:37:53.710
We'd be in huge trouble.

00:37:53.793 --> 00:37:55.837
I won't. Don't worry.

00:37:55.920 --> 00:37:59.090
You're the only one
who got a special discount.

00:37:59.173 --> 00:38:01.634
All the other owners paid the full price.

00:38:01.718 --> 00:38:02.635
Do you understand?

00:38:05.638 --> 00:38:06.723
Thank you.

00:38:07.891 --> 00:38:08.766
Thanks.

00:38:21.195 --> 00:38:23.823
COMING SOON: PEDIATRICS, DENTISTRY
PHARMACY, RESTAURANT, DERMATOLOGY

00:38:23.907 --> 00:38:25.867
Welcome. I've been waiting for you.

00:38:25.950 --> 00:38:27.827
There are too many people waiting.

00:38:27.911 --> 00:38:29.579
If you sign the contract now…

00:38:30.121 --> 00:38:31.289
The subway station is…

00:38:31.372 --> 00:38:33.333
I really can't go below 1.2 billion won.

00:38:33.416 --> 00:38:34.792
This place is a real bargain.

00:38:34.876 --> 00:38:36.336
That's as low as we can go.

00:39:00.234 --> 00:39:02.028
I don't need the company anymore.

00:39:03.237 --> 00:39:04.781
Ten-million-a-month Nak-su.

00:39:05.281 --> 00:39:06.658
Ten-million-a-month Nak-su!

00:39:09.869 --> 00:39:12.455
Ten-million-a-month Nak-su!

00:39:16.084 --> 00:39:18.836
Where have you been?
You didn't even answer your phone.

00:39:19.921 --> 00:39:22.298
What is this?
You should eat a proper meal.

00:39:22.382 --> 00:39:24.258
I was going to eat out with you.

00:39:24.342 --> 00:39:26.177
But you didn't pick up your phone.

00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:27.178
Where's Su-gyeom?

00:39:27.261 --> 00:39:29.180
Su-gyeom? He went out.

00:39:30.556 --> 00:39:31.641
-Honey.
-Yes?

00:39:35.937 --> 00:39:39.315
What are you doing? Hey!
What's with you? Honey!

00:39:39.399 --> 00:39:41.150
Hon--

00:39:41.234 --> 00:39:42.527
Stop! Stop it!

00:39:48.741 --> 00:39:50.660
-Welcome.
-Oh my.

00:39:51.786 --> 00:39:52.954
Welcome, sir.

00:39:53.037 --> 00:39:54.455
Is business going well?

00:39:54.539 --> 00:39:55.540
Yes.

00:39:56.541 --> 00:39:58.376
This is huge.

00:39:58.459 --> 00:40:00.086
Is this place really yours, Dad?

00:40:01.754 --> 00:40:03.965
Could you bring three coffees
over to that table?

00:40:04.048 --> 00:40:06.384
Sure. I'll make them for you myself.

00:40:06.467 --> 00:40:07.760
-All right.
-Yes.

00:40:09.679 --> 00:40:10.888
Please have a seat.

00:40:12.181 --> 00:40:15.309
This is really nice.

00:40:15.393 --> 00:40:17.729
-That's your problem, Jin-woo.
-I'm sorry.

00:40:17.812 --> 00:40:18.896
Oh my.

00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:20.148
Well!

00:40:20.231 --> 00:40:21.607
-Goodness.
-Look who it is.

00:40:21.691 --> 00:40:22.692
-Sir.
-Oh my.

00:40:22.775 --> 00:40:25.153
-Hello.
-My light, my joy.

00:40:25.236 --> 00:40:27.155
-Jeez.
-My brilliant strategist.

00:40:27.739 --> 00:40:28.740
Goodness.

00:40:28.823 --> 00:40:30.033
Congratulations on the opening.

00:40:30.116 --> 00:40:30.992
CONGRATULATIONS

00:40:31.075 --> 00:40:32.910
Put it down somewhere over there.

00:40:32.994 --> 00:40:34.829
-Hey.
-Not there.

00:40:34.912 --> 00:40:35.913
Down there. On the floor.

00:40:35.997 --> 00:40:37.540
-You punk.
-There.

00:40:37.623 --> 00:40:39.208
He can be slow to catch on.

00:40:39.292 --> 00:40:40.960
How are things at the company?

00:40:41.627 --> 00:40:44.797
Nothing gets done without you, Nak-su.

00:40:45.339 --> 00:40:48.092
Can't you come back to the team?

00:40:48.176 --> 00:40:49.719
I'll treat you really well.

00:40:49.802 --> 00:40:52.722
I'm just so sick of being a wage slave.

00:40:52.805 --> 00:40:54.348
Don't you agree, Jin-woo?

00:40:54.432 --> 00:40:56.851
All this time,
I failed to see your grand vision.

00:40:56.934 --> 00:40:58.352
-I apologize, sir.
-Hey!

00:40:58.436 --> 00:40:59.479
Cut the crap.

00:40:59.562 --> 00:41:01.314
Go get us some coffee.

00:41:01.939 --> 00:41:03.274
-With my own money?
-No.

00:41:03.357 --> 00:41:04.776
Just put it on my tab.

00:41:04.859 --> 00:41:05.818
Get whatever you want.

00:41:05.902 --> 00:41:07.403
Thank you, sir.

00:41:07.487 --> 00:41:08.529
Good lord.

00:41:09.405 --> 00:41:11.741
I am really sorry about last time.

00:41:11.824 --> 00:41:14.410
It's fine. You were only trying
to give me good advice.

00:41:14.494 --> 00:41:16.287
I apologize, Mr. Baek.

00:41:16.370 --> 00:41:17.747
I'm sorry.

00:41:18.414 --> 00:41:21.167
Why are you being like this? Come on.

00:41:21.250 --> 00:41:23.711
Just call me by my name like you used to.

00:41:23.795 --> 00:41:24.670
Do it.

00:41:25.379 --> 00:41:28.508
Honey, just say it once, please.

00:41:33.387 --> 00:41:34.972
Jeong-tae.

00:41:35.056 --> 00:41:36.057
You love it.

00:41:37.892 --> 00:41:38.810
Nak-su!

00:41:38.893 --> 00:41:40.478
Hello, everyone!

00:41:41.562 --> 00:41:42.980
-Who's this?
-Oh, hey.

00:41:43.564 --> 00:41:46.442
So this is the life of a real man.

00:41:46.526 --> 00:41:48.111
I respect you, Nak-su.

00:41:49.028 --> 00:41:53.407
Ha-jin, I was out of line last time.

00:41:53.908 --> 00:41:55.535
I've been reflecting on my actions.

00:41:55.618 --> 00:41:57.245
I'm truly sorry.

00:41:57.787 --> 00:41:59.914
Okay, just put it down over there.

00:42:00.414 --> 00:42:01.374
Mr. Kim!

00:42:01.457 --> 00:42:02.458
Hey!

00:42:03.167 --> 00:42:04.293
-Hey, guys.
-Hello, sir.

00:42:05.586 --> 00:42:06.963
We heard the good news.

00:42:07.630 --> 00:42:10.716
I guess all my time spent
on real estate stuff was for nothing.

00:42:10.800 --> 00:42:11.676
This is our staff.

00:42:11.759 --> 00:42:13.511
You're on another level, sir.

00:42:13.594 --> 00:42:15.429
Have you all eaten yet?

00:42:15.513 --> 00:42:16.472
No, we haven't.

00:42:16.556 --> 00:42:18.891
Take this and get whatever you want.

00:42:18.975 --> 00:42:21.477
Come back here for coffee afterward.

00:42:21.561 --> 00:42:24.397
Really? Then can we order

00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:26.399
-the large Ttokdari combo meal?
-Hey!

00:42:26.482 --> 00:42:28.192
Go to the premium beef spot right across.

00:42:28.276 --> 00:42:30.736
Treat yourself to the chef's top cuts.

00:42:30.820 --> 00:42:32.405
Thank you so much.

00:42:32.488 --> 00:42:33.906
-Thank you.
-And congratulations.

00:42:33.990 --> 00:42:36.367
-We'll be there. Please join us.
-Okay.

00:42:36.450 --> 00:42:38.369
-I'll head over too.
-Sung-gu, hi.

00:42:38.452 --> 00:42:39.537
What the heck?

00:42:39.620 --> 00:42:40.788
What…

00:42:41.831 --> 00:42:44.917
-What are you doing? Hurry up!
-Okay. Here's your coffee.

00:42:45.001 --> 00:42:46.919
-All right.
-Hand them out.

00:42:47.003 --> 00:42:48.713
-I'm sorry.
-Just hand them out.

00:42:48.796 --> 00:42:50.506
-Here you go.
-Put them all down.

00:42:52.175 --> 00:42:53.342
Here you go.

00:42:53.426 --> 00:42:54.510
Sir.

00:42:54.594 --> 00:42:56.387
I have some prostate issues.

00:42:56.470 --> 00:42:58.264
So can I have a tomato sandwich?

00:42:59.015 --> 00:43:00.808
Sure. Go ahead.

00:43:00.892 --> 00:43:02.894
You're too young for that.
Must be from the stress.

00:43:02.977 --> 00:43:04.645
I guess your thing is practically useless.

00:43:04.729 --> 00:43:06.731
Oh my. I guess you're right.

00:43:06.814 --> 00:43:10.109
Well, it's not alcohol,
but how about a toast?

00:43:10.193 --> 00:43:11.652
Now…

00:43:13.279 --> 00:43:14.322
All right.

00:43:15.156 --> 00:43:17.158
-To Mr. Kim!
-Congratulations!

00:43:26.751 --> 00:43:28.252
"Cheers"? Yeah, right.

00:43:33.633 --> 00:43:34.550
Honey?

00:43:34.634 --> 00:43:36.677
-Yeah, keep on dreaming.
-Honey.

00:43:38.262 --> 00:43:40.723
Receiving your severance as a pension
rather than a lump sum

00:43:40.806 --> 00:43:43.768
-would be better for taxes.
-Please close the account.

00:43:43.851 --> 00:43:44.727
Okay.

00:43:44.810 --> 00:43:47.230
I'd also like to apply
for a personal loan.

00:43:47.313 --> 00:43:48.981
A personal loan?

00:43:49.065 --> 00:43:51.609
Then please fill out this form.

00:43:51.692 --> 00:43:53.152
All right.

00:43:53.236 --> 00:43:56.906
OPENING SOON

00:43:56.989 --> 00:43:58.491
-Really?
-I mean it.

00:43:58.574 --> 00:44:00.618
-You've made an excellent choice.
-I knew it.

00:44:00.701 --> 00:44:01.869
Yes, I understand.

00:44:01.953 --> 00:44:03.746
I'll let you know
if a unit becomes available.

00:44:03.829 --> 00:44:05.790
You have arrived at your destination.

00:44:05.873 --> 00:44:06.749
Let's see!

00:44:06.832 --> 00:44:08.542
TIME TAKEN: 3 MINUTES 56 SECONDS

00:44:08.626 --> 00:44:11.587
Only three minutes from the station,
even if I walk slowly.

00:44:11.671 --> 00:44:12.922
All right!

00:44:13.673 --> 00:44:15.258
You'll be opening soon!

00:44:21.681 --> 00:44:24.433
Let's see. What could that be?

00:44:25.184 --> 00:44:26.852
